      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Large, diverse compound libraries are an essential requisite in target-based drug development. In this work, a robust microwave-assisted synthesis for the diastereoselective generation of 3-saccharinyl-trans-β-lactams is reported. The method is optimised for combinatorial library synthesis in which decoration of the scaffold is varied on both the β-lactam and the saccharine moiety. Within the European Lead Factory (ELF) consortium, a library of 263 compounds was efficiently produced using the developed methodology."
      },
